note: written
keeps: undefined | nothing | no reason
bars: \bwhich\b[^.]*\bwhich\b | \bthat\b[^.]*\bthat\b | \bits catalog entry\b | \bmismatchof\b
why: Kirill found a summary with a relative clause inside a relative clause hard to read; a summary holds one relative clause at most, so what the function returns and when it returns nothing each stay in one clause
labelled: 2026-09-30
--- code
export function mismatchOf(statement: Statement, catalog: Catalog): string | undefined {
  const listed = catalog.closingBalance(statement.account);
  if (listed === statement.closingBalance) {
    return undefined;
  }
  return `closing balance ${statement.closingBalance} is not the listed ${listed}`;
}
--- facts
The catalog lists a closing balance for each account.
A statement whose closing balance is not that listed balance is reported with the reason, and a statement that matches it gives no reason.
